# World Cup sweepstake manual updates

When asked to update the World Cup sweepstake scores:

- Use `app/data/world-cup-fantasy.ts` and append to `WORLD_CUP_FANTASY_MANUAL_MATCHES`.
- Only look for **newly finished** World Cup matches that are not already in the manual ledger.
- Do **not** re-check or re-verify matches already recorded in `WORLD_CUP_FANTASY_MANUAL_MATCHES`; those entries are the source of truth.
- When checking external score sources, use each assigned team's code, display name, and `searchNames` variants from `WORLD_CUP_TEAM_BY_CODE` / `getWorldCupTeamSearchTerms()` so alternate spellings are not missed (for example Ivory Coast / Côte d'Ivoire, Cape Verde / Cabo Verde, Turkey / Türkiye, South Korea / Korea Republic, Iran / IR Iran).
- Add only final results: home/away teams, final goals, and red-card tallies for each team.
- Count red-card dismissals in the tally, including second-yellow dismissals where reported.
- Keep `WORLD_CUP_FANTASY_FIXTURES` fresh whenever adding scores. If a newly recorded result means an upcoming fixture has just finished or disappeared from the “Today’s upcoming fixtures” box, add the next known upcoming sweepstake fixture(s) for the current UTC day so the box above the standings keeps rolling forward with managers involved.
- Do not manually edit player totals or standings. The app applies the scoring rules from `WORLD_CUP_FANTASY_SCORING` via `computeStandings()`:
  - 3 pts win
  - 1 pt draw
  - +1 for 3+ goals
  - -1 for 3+ conceded
  - -1 per red card
- After adding or changing any ledger entry, run `npm run world-cup:standings` and use that computed output as the only source for player totals, leader/bottom claims, and tie wording in both `WORLD_CUP_FANTASY_DAILY_UPDATE` and the final summary. Do not calculate standings in your head, infer them from the latest match only, or write phrases like “leads on X”, “level on X”, “bottom on X”, or “up to X” unless the number/name pairing appears in the computed standings output.
- If no new matches are finished, leave the ledger unchanged.
- Keep `WORLD_CUP_FANTASY_DAILY_UPDATE` fresh whenever the table changes. It appears above the standings as “Daily roast”; make it current, relevant, and funny in a broad British football-roast voice: dry, cutting, and never too American-sports-banter. Vary the comic frame across football misery, tactical incompetence, Sunday-league chaos, pundit nonsense, group-chat humiliation, doomed press conferences, bad defending, hopeless substitutions, travel-sick minnows, and general scoreboard embarrassment. Pub imagery is allowed occasionally, but do not default to landlords, pints, bar stools, last orders, or the same pub-table setup. It can be harsh and rude as part of the joke, but keep the punches aimed at sweepstake performance, teams, and footballing incompetence rather than personal cruelty. Summarise all recorded sweepstake matches from that GMT calendar day, not just the latest match appended, so earlier results do not vanish from the narrative. Roast whoever is bottom according to `npm run world-cup:standings`, and blame the teams that lost or underperformed that day; if recent summaries, git history, or the current ledger clearly show someone has been stuck bottom for several updates/days, lean into that running joke without inventing unsupported history. Vary the phrasing so the same joke or stock phrase does not appear every update. Player names and assigned team names are optional seasoning: use them sparingly when they improve the joke, not in every line by default.
- When summarising an update, include the current league table and mirror the same fresh, relevant, British-toned roast from the Daily roast section.
- This request is normally intended to update the live site. After adding score-only ledger updates and verifying the app still builds, push the change through to `origin/main` unless the user explicitly asks for PR-only work or says not to deploy.
- If a feature branch was used first, fast-forward `main` from it rather than leaving the update only on the feature branch:
  `git checkout main && git pull origin main && git merge --ff-only <score-update-branch> && git push -u origin main`.

